''Note: Pet level = Character level. A quasi rule gives +17% PAP per pet level. Scaling math: 1.17 ^ (log(cxp) / log(1.09)) = cxp ^ (log(1.17) / log(1.09)) = 1.822. Because PAP is ^2, ^1.822^2 = ^(1.822 * 2) = 3.319, then phylacteries add about ^0.6. Therefore the final Cexp scaling is about ^3.9''

==Attributes==
* Fill for items<br/>(Requires quite a lot - {{ItemTooltip|Blessed Tapestry}} is your friend for 1sec points)
* Important Perks
* Max everything except for SPC, DOM and WIS which are left at 240+10.<br/>(For DOM, invest in Vers until you have enough points to respec on exile for the 150/250 perks. Until then, you'll get more profit from the Vers points)
* Finally invest in Vers

Chronomancer is one of the few classes that does not profit from clicks but can generate enough autoclicks for the dominance 150/250 perks to outweigh that many points in Versatility.  The threshold is in the range of e13-e16 clicks.

''NOTE: SPC provides very little - Need 250 for Kilt in snap, next is 175 for Perfected Kata in buildup, it may be better to invest 175 points in SPC and forgo Kilt. Needs testing.''

