==Phases==
A typical run consists of
* Quick Burst Phase to get upgrades and sources.
* Careful Pet Level (Be able to still cast Time Fork)
* Stack Time Fork
* Pet Levelling phase (As much as possible so you can no longer cast TF)
* Skip Time
* Void Mana Phase
* Burst Phase

===Careful Pet Levelling Set===
{| class="wikitable" style= "max-width:800px"
|-
! Goal
| Stack your pet levels by casting {{SpellTooltip|Time Fork}} until the spell's level requirement is about 10-20 levels lower than you character's base level (what it reverts to after casting Time Fork). 
|}

{{Callout|
class=warning|'''Do not raise your pet level too high''' or you won't be able to stack Time Fork in the next phase for the remainder of the exile..}}

{{GuideBox
|spells=#0#PetXP[Careful]@208,0;29,2;60,2;111,2;68,1;104,2
|items=#0#PetXP[Careful]@104;101;2;29;14;32;40;68;56;84;70;1022;209;304;411;415;91;2007;3001}}

* We need some Shard enchant gear to keep everything up at the Spell Memetic range.
* {{SpellTooltip|Ritual Of Power}} and {{SpellTooltip|Ritual Of Potency}} have minimal impact, but can allow for slightly more sources and thus a higher baseline character level.  You can replace them with better spells as your base character level improves.
* You do not need to be super aggressive about getting as close to the limit as you can.  As soon as you have enough Compressed Time per second to sustain both Time Fork and Wormhole in the next phase you can move on.  Likewise, I advise against using any mythics or other strategies to boost your character level in this phase.

===Spell Stacking Set===
{| class="wikitable" style= "max-width:800px"
|-
! Goal
| Stacking Time Fork, stacking Accumulated spells, and casting lots of spells to charge {{ItemTooltip|The Accumulator}}
|}

{{GuideBox
|spells=#1#Buildup[TimeFork50%]@208,2;60,2;17,2;104,2;33,2;66,2
|items=#1#Buildup[TimeFork50%]@101;104;2;29;14;32;41;68;56;86;77;1022;209;307;416;415;90;2007;3003;509}}

* Spend about 50% of buildup time here.

Some gear optimizations are available.
* You need enough Compressed Time or Pet Ability Power gear for {{SpellTooltip|Time Fork}} and  {{SpellTooltip|Wormhole}} while also having enough Shard Gear to keep {{SpellTooltip|Ritual Of Power}} and {{SpellTooltip|Superposition}} going at peak cast rate at higher Spell Memetic levels.
* You may need to swap some combination of {{ItemTooltip|Daemonics Reverse-Engineering}} for {{ItemTooltip|Spell Shards Fractalization}} or {{ItemTooltip|Inquisitive Eye}} for {{ItemTooltip|Pheromone Gland}}. {{ItemTooltip|Perfected Kata Bracers}} for {{ItemTooltip|Precise Wristband}} is also possible, but should be avoided.
* {{ItemTooltip|Ritual Disk}} is the best mount for this phase, but if you don't have it {{ItemTooltip|The Rubedo Engine}} is only marginally worse (about 0.3 of an E) after you account for the different scalings of RoP and Superposition.
* {{ItemTooltip|Temporal Scabbard}} doubles the rate at which you stack {{SpellTooltip|Ritual Of Potency}} and makes RoPot your best scaling burst spell. It scales better than both regular and enhanced {{SpellTooltip|Ritual Of Power}} (^0.8 per cast rather than ^0.45 or ^0.55) and gains charges based on EVERY spell cast. This will be dominated by accumulated spells due to the Heritage upgrade "muscle memory" multiplying accumulated casts.
* All of this combines to wanting to sit on this phase for roughly 50% of your total exile length with the remaining 50% being spent on the Time Skip phase.

===Pet Levelling Set===
{| class="wikitable" style= "max-width:800px"
|-
! Goal
| Stack as many pet levels as possible. A class ability makes Pet Ability Power scale 1.17^PetLevel, and PAP is ^2 to profit, so every extra level is very strong.
|}

{{GuideBox
|spells=#8#PetXP@208,2;29,2;60,2;71,2;66,2;67,2
|items=#8#PetXP@104;113;4;29;14;31;43;66;57;86;74;1022;212;300;415;405;90;2008;3005;508}}

{{Note| You really want to use {{ItemTooltip|Endtimes Failsafe}} here. Even better with a CharXP imbuement.}}

* Character level -> Pet level. Actually, {{SpellTooltip|Time Fork}}'s level requirement = pet level and *casting* TF earns you pet levels. Therefore higher character level (or level requirement reduction) means more pet levels. But because TF resets all sources of "collectible" character experience, once TF requires more than your base character level from static sources (like mana sources), it will auto-remove itself from your spellbar. So you'll need to spam this set to put TF *back* on the spellbar. 
* You can squeeze a handful of extra pet levels even after spamming the set to up TF back no longer works. Toggle back and forth with the Time Skip phase and it'll give you a large chunk of void entities and autoclicks that will continue to boost your character level when you switch back to this set. Do this until spending 30-60 seconds on Time Skip doesn't earn you another pet level. On longer exiles it's probably technically worth micromanaging this a bit more to earn another few levels even if they take a few minutes each... but who has time for that?
* If you have the Triumph Ingot Shortage, it's a good idea to enchant the Mystery Power enchant gear; {{ItemTooltip|Recaller Stone}} and {{ItemTooltip|Broomstaff Of Klevdariah}} to get a few more pet levels out of your pet {{PetTooltip|Temporal Paradox}}. This is useful when pushing for Delusions.
* This spell and item set have been numbered to put them on shortcut key 9. This is intentionally "out of the way" to reduce the chance of a misclick accidentally turning on this set and overleveling your {{SpellTooltip|Time Fork}}.

